A||||5||skitime||What colors were 88 Fieros?||||1||
Z||000000||skitime||12-03-2000||06:37 PM||||Does anyone know where to find all the actual colors the 88s were produced. Better yet, do you know where to go to see color chips. How common were each color?||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||12-03-2000||08:29 PM||||I am have looked at a 1988 GT T-Top to buy but am not familiar with this color burgandy. I am sure it is orginal but I want to be sure. Is it common or rare? Any pictures of this color on a Fiero in pristine condition would be helpful in deciding to get this car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||12-03-2000||08:40 PM||||You mean like this T-top's color:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gt2_1.jpg"> <P>It is factory  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||12-03-2000||08:42 PM||||Burgundy is called medium red metallic. It is a factory color and was introduced in 1987 ( a TON of '87s are this color).  <P>Here's a list os available colors in '88:<P>-black<BR>-bright red<BR>-medium red metallic<BR>-yellow<BR>-silver<BR>-white<P>Silver and yellow are the rarest colors (for '88) followed by medium red metallic, black, white & red. <P>I have owned one of each color!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I've had a yellow Formula, a bright red Formula, a medium red metallic Formula, a few black GT's, a white Formula, a silver GT & Formula.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||12-03-2000||08:42 PM||||The actual color name is Medium Metallic Red.<BR>The color was available for 87 and 88 model years. Don't have any pics of one. I think the colors for 88's are<BR>Bright Red<BR>Black<BR>White<BR>Med. Met. Red<BR>Yellow (Only 1988 color)<BR>Met Gray (Silver)<P>Metallic Gold was 86 and 87<BR>Blue was 1987 only.||||reg||1
Z||000005||skitime||12-03-2000||09:02 PM||||The car appeared slightly browner in color than the picture posted by Cooter.  I know colors change by cameras and monitors but there was definitely metallic in the paint.  ||||reg||1
